\f1\fs22 \'93The Wheel of Death!\'94 they responded. \'93Wheel\'85of\'85Death. Wheel\'85of\'85Death.\'94\
The Wheel of Death was wheeled out by a pretty extra in an elaborate headdress and swimsuit.\
\'93Well, c\'92mon,\'94 Alexander chided Eloise. \'93Spin the wheel.\'94\
\'93I would if you unbound my arms,\'94 Eloise answered.\
\'93That\'92s just like you isn\'92t it? Always trying to negotiate your way out of everything.\'94\
\'93Go tax yourself, Alexander. I\'92ve already written you out of my will. Everything goes to\'97\'94\
\'93Yes, I already know\'97the evil resurrection of the undead son, Bill Clinton.\'94\
\'93Spin the wheel! Spin the wheel! Spin the wheel!\'94 the chorus ascended over the stomping of feet.\
\'93Shall I?\'94 Alexander offered.\
\'93By all means,\'94 Eloise answered.\
Alexander spun. All the muscle necks in the audience held their breaths. The wheel spun through its enticing options, slowed, even to the point that viewers could make guesses about where it would land.\
\'93Shark tank!\'94 Alexander announced with a gameshow smile.\
The audience bayed and cheered. A curtain was drawn back and there it stood, with all the eerie, hypnotic power of a huge tank of studio-light-diffracting water\'97sparkling and glistening\'97with half a dozen young and hungry bull sharks patrolling in it.\
Eloise took a large, nervous breath and began to wonder if the script actually ended with her as chum in it.\
