\cf2 A pregnant woman walked heavily from backstage to behind Eloise\'92s chair and put her hands on her shoulders.\
The rent-a-boofhead audience looked her over with patriarchal possessiveness. Pregnancy means obedient. Somebody had done well with her, and she deserved deferential respect for knowing her place as a vessel.\
\'93Hello, Alexander.\'94\
\'93Sarah!\'94 Alexander turned to the audience. \'93Everyone, this is my lovely wife.\'94\
The men applauded Alexander.\
\'93This is the grandmother of my son,\'94 Sarah told the audience.\
Back in their townhouse, the Sages were somewhat miffed by that reinterpretation.\
For the jarheads in the auditorium, it complicated things. They hadn\'92t minded executing a former employer, but career dads like themselves never know when they might need a free babysitter to look after the kids.\
While the audience ogled the yummy mummy, Hayley appeared behind Alexander and put a gun to his head.\
Guns from the audience quickly trained on her, but she knew how to use Alexander for cover. Men leaned into the aisles and stood in each other\'92s way. Whichever way they looked at it, they would have to shoot through their host.\
