The audience hurled abuse at Hayley. They told her to put the gun down. They described where they would put it for her. One offered to show her how he shoots at home. As she moved Alexander across the stage, pistols and guns lined her up, though no one could get a bead on her without risking hitting the aquarium. None of them wanted to be eaten by sharks.\
\'93Put the gun down, sweetheart!\'94\
Hayley steered Alexander to Eloise and Sarah, who drew him into an awkward hug. The necks watched a woman cuddle their boss while another held a gun to his head. Many had complaints about their own marriages, but nothing like this.\
Sarah spoke close to Alexander\'92s ear, though his microphone shared it with everybody.\
\'93We\'92re all going backstage together.\'94\
\'93Okay, I think I see where you\'92re going with this.\'94 Alexander nodded, grazing his head on the muzzle of Hayley\'92s pistol. \
\'93Push your mother\'92s chair. Hayley will come with you. I\'92ll be right beside you.\'94\
Alexander glanced at the audience.\
\'93Tell them,\'94 Sarah said.\
\'93Lower your weapons,\'94 Alexander called, his voice cracking.\
Few did. The guns considered shooting. The bitch with the gun was an easier target now; Eloise had always been an open target, but nobody wanted to explain how they had killed Alexander\'92s heir while defending his right to kill his mother.\
Sarah put Alexander\'92s hands on the back of Eloise\'92s chair.\
\'93Come on.\'94\
The chair began to roll. Sarah stayed beside the chair. Hayley kept her gun on Alexander.\
A neck halfway back in the audience was muttering parts of the Sages\'92 ditty to himself.  \'93Praise the Duck Prince. He\'92s the One after the One. The Holy Momma\'85\'94\
